## License, End User License Agreement, and Terms of Service for RoxStar

**License Version 2.0 and Effective Date 12-05-2026.**

---

### Preamble and Disclosure of Intent

This project is a clean-room, fan-made reimplementation of the server-side API that once powered Moshi Monsters, a game originally created and owned by Mind Candy Ltd. It was built entirely from independent research, observation, and reverse engineering of publicly observable behaviour — no proprietary source code, internal documentation, or confidential assets belonging to Mind Candy were used or accessed in its creation.

Moshi Monsters was officially discontinued in 2019. This project exists solely to preserve the experience of a game for the people who grew up with it. It is a labour of love, not a commercial venture, and carries no intention to infringe upon, replace, or misrepresent the original work or its creators.

Mind Candy Ltd retains all intellectual property rights to the Moshi Monsters name, branding, characters, assets, and associated trademarks. This project makes no claim to any of those rights.

---

## 1. Definitions

- **"The Software"** means this repository and all source code, documentation, and configuration files contained within it.
- **"You"** means any individual or entity accessing, using, copying, modifying, or distributing the Software.
- **"Original Work"** means the *Moshi Monsters* game, service, and associated intellectual property owned by Mind Candy Ltd.
- **"Instances"** means any deployment or hosting of the Software.
- **"Public Instance"** means any deployment of the Software that is accessible to users outside of your own household or private network.
- **"Commercial Use"** means any use of the Software in exchange for monetary compensation, or as part of a product or service sold or monetised in any form.
- **"Corresponding Source"** means the complete source code necessary for users to build, run, and modify the Software, including all scripts, configuration, and build tooling required to reproduce any deployed instance.

