## 12. Interpretation

Where the terms of this Agreement are ambiguous, they shall be construed in accordance with the following principles, which reflect the intent of the authors and form part of the Agreement:

- **Preservation over exploitation.** This license is designed to enable good-faith preservation of a discontinued game. Uses that serve that goal are to be read permissively; uses that exploit the Software or the Original Work commercially or deceptively are to be read restrictively.
- **User clarity.** Any ambiguity about whether a disclosure or attribution obligation has been met shall be resolved in favour of the interpretation that better informs users of the Software's unofficial, fan-made nature.
- **Source availability.** Any ambiguity about whether the Corresponding Source obligation in Section 3 has been triggered shall be resolved in favour of requiring disclosure.

These principles do not override the plain meaning of any provision, but shall guide interpretation where the plain meaning is genuinely unclear.

